## §2 Applicability

This methodology applies when:

- <applicability condition 1 — e.g. "the system has long-lived business logic separable from infrastructure">
- <applicability condition 2>
- <applicability condition 3>

This methodology does **NOT** apply (and forcing it produces over-built code) when:

- <non-applicability condition 1 — e.g. "the work is a one-shot exploratory script">
- <non-applicability condition 2 — e.g. "the module is a thin DTO mapping with no behaviour">
- <non-applicability condition 3 — e.g. "the deadline forces a known-throwaway prototype">

The "when NOT to apply" half is non-negotiable. If you cannot bound the methodology's applicability, the doctrine is too broad and will be wrongly applied. Re-read the primary source for scope claims before shipping the handbook.

## §3 Red flags

